.\" EXT2 driver man page
.TH EXT2 4 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Special Files"
.SH NAME
ext2 \- Second Extended Filesystem driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount -t ext2
.I device mountpoint
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B ext2
driver provides read-write support for the Second Extended Filesystem (ext2).
It supports standard Unix file operations including file creation, deletion, reading, writing, and directory management.
.SS Features
.IP \[bu] 2
Support for both Rev 0 (old) and Rev 1 (dynamic) inode sizes.
.IP \[bu]
Block groups and block group descriptors.
.IP \[bu]
Indirect, double indirect, and triple indirect block addressing.
.IP \[bu]
Directory iteration (readdir).
.IP \[bu]
Symbolic links (fast and slow).
.SS Concurrency
The driver is designed to be thread-safe for concurrent access:
.TP
.B I/O Buffers
All block I/O operations use dynamically allocated buffers (via
.BR kmalloc (9))
to prevent race conditions when multiple threads access the filesystem simultaneously.
.TP
.B Directory Iteration
Directory iteration state (current position, directory entry buffer) is maintained within the node context
.RB ( struct ext2_node_t ),
ensuring that concurrent
.BR readdir (3)
calls on different file descriptors do not interfere with each other.
.SS Structures
The driver defines the following on-disk structures in
.IR ext2.h :
.TP
.B ext2_superblock_t
Filesystem global metadata (magic number, block count, inode count).
.TP
.B ext2_group_desc_t
Block group descriptor pointing to bitmaps and tables.
.TP
.B ext2_inode_t
Inode structure containing file metadata and block pointers.
.TP
.B ext2_dirent_t
Directory entry structure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I sys/fs/ext2/ext2.h
Structure definitions.
.TP
.I sys/fs/ext2/ext2.c
Implementation of the filesystem driver.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vfs (9),
.BR mount (2)
